; Play-Quake - Quake III Arena with the GLES2 renderer on ogles2 (no gl4es), to play (not timed).
;   CD to the ogles2-m6-5 directory, then:   Execute Play-Quake
;   With the game elsewhere:   Execute Play-Quake Q3DATA=<the directory with baseq3>
;   No tearing (vsync; at most the display's 60 fps, 30 when a frame takes
;   longer than a refresh):    Execute Play-Quake VSYNC=1
; Full screen 640x480 at first; the menu's System settings offer every 32-bit
; screen mode (compiled shaders come with the package for 640x480 and
; 1920x1080; other modes compile theirs once, about 90 s, with a progress
; bar). The frame rate
; is shown at the top right, sound through
; AHI (16 bit; the engine falls back to Paula if AHI does not start).
; The game's own files (config, logs) go to home/ here; nothing is written
; to the game's directory. Quit from the game's menu (Escape, Exit).
.key Q3DATA/K,VSYNC/K
.def VSYNC 0
.def Q3DATA "Stuff:Quake3-68k-beta10/Quake3-68k-beta10"
.bra {
.ket }

FailAt 21
If NOT EXISTS libs/ogles2.library
  Echo "Please CD into the ogles2-m6-5 directory first,"
  Echo "then run:  Execute Play-Quake"
  Quit 20
EndIf
If NOT EXISTS "{Q3DATA}/baseq3/pak0.pk3"
  Echo "No Quake III data at {Q3DATA}/baseq3: run Execute Play-Quake Q3DATA=<directory>"
  Quit 20
EndIf

Assign M6R5: ""
If NOT EXISTS M6R5:cache
  MakeDir M6R5:cache
EndIf
Assign LIBS: M6R5:libs ADD
Assign OGLES2Cache: M6R5:cache
; The modules load from the current directory.
CD M6R5:bin
M6R5:bin/quake3-gl2 +set fs_basepath "{Q3DATA}" +set fs_homepath M6R5:home +set r_fullscreen 1 +set r_mode 3 +set r_swapInterval {VSYNC} +set cg_drawFPS 1
CD M6R5:
Assign OGLES2Cache:
Assign LIBS: M6R5:libs REMOVE
Assign M6R5:
